# I18n

## Framework semantics

CakePHP I18n uses message catalogs (`resources/locales`), `__()` / `__d()` helpers, and locale switching. Prefer framework I18n over inventing translation packages foreign to the app.

## Required behavior

- Wrap user-facing strings with the project’s I18n helpers when the app is localized.
- Keep message domains/catalogs organized; do not hardcode every language in controllers.
- Format dates/numbers with I18n-aware formatters when locale matters.
- Do not invent Laravel `__()` / lang JSON layouts as a parallel system.

## Anti-patterns

- Parallel translation systems beside CakePHP I18n without cause
- Translating only in templates while API messages stay English-hardcoded inconsistently (follow project)

## Review checklist

- [ ] New user-facing strings follow project I18n conventions
- [ ] Locale catalogs updated when required
